From: K7 Yocto Integration <k7@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] rockchip: use Python 3 for BL31 and stop on decoding failure

The decoder already uses Python 3 compatible bytes and struct operations.
Use the native interpreter supplied by Yocto. Propagate decoding errors so
the generator cannot silently produce a FIT without its ATF nodes.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [Yocto integration of vendor BSP]

diff --git a/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/decode_bl31.py b/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/decode_bl31.py
--- a/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/decode_bl31.py
+++ b/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/decode_bl31.py
@@ -1,4 +1,4 @@
-#!/usr/bin/env python2
+#!/usr/bin/env python3
 #
 # Copyright (C) 2020 Rockchip Electronics Co., Ltd
 #
diff --git a/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/fit_nodes.sh b/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/fit_nodes.sh
--- a/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/fit_nodes.sh
+++ b/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/fit_nodes.sh
@@ -110,7 +110,7 @@
 
 function gen_bl31_node()
 {
-	${srctree}/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/decode_bl31.py
+	${srctree}/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/decode_bl31.py || exit 1
 
 	NUM=1
 	for ATF in `ls -1 -S bl31_0x*.bin`
